# .mutation-allowlist - surviving (LIVED) mutants accepted as already known.
#
# Format:  <MUTATOR> <file>:<line>
#
# Add an entry ONLY when the mutant is provably equivalent (no test can ever kill it,
# because the mutation does not change observable behaviour) or the gap is a conscious,
# accepted risk. Adding a real test gap here hides a real risk, and mutation testing
# exists precisely to surface those.
#
# The comparison is BY LINE: an entry naming the file at another line does not cover the
# mutant that appeared there after a refactor.
#
# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY: 0 entries so far. Seed it with `make mutate` (whole module) and
# commit only the survivors that run proves are already known.
